# cppcheck suppressions baseline for wrq.
# Run via: make cppcheck
# Do not leave a bare `#` on a line. cppcheck 2.10 strips the comment marker,
# finds an empty id, and aborts the whole run.

# Goal: a clean run so genuinely new findings stand out during code work.
# Only third-party code and project-convention style noise are muted here.
# CI runs an older cppcheck than a current Homebrew install, so entries that
# exist only to satisfy one version say so.

# --- Third-party vendored sources. Upstream owns these, not this repo. ---
# Redis event loop and allocator.
*:src/ae.c
*:src/ae_epoll.c
*:src/ae_evport.c
*:src/ae_kqueue.c
*:src/ae_select.c
*:src/zmalloc.c
# HdrHistogram.
*:src/hdr_histogram.c
# Node.js HTTP parser.
*:src/http_parser.c
# TinyMT PRNG.
*:src/tinymt64.c
*:src/tinymt64.h

# --- Project-convention style noise (not defects). ---
# Functions are declared with unnamed params in headers, named in definitions.
funcArgNamesDifferentUnnamed
funcArgNamesDifferent
# const-correctness suggestions on pointers. Stylistic only.
constParameterPointer
constVariablePointer

# --- Reviewed pre-existing findings in first-party code. ---
# These are line-specific on purpose. If a line shifts, the finding reappears
# rather than being silently hidden, so it gets re-reviewed.
# False positive: `units` is passed to format_units() on the next line.
unreadVariable:src/units.c:86
unreadVariable:src/units.c:89
# `&` binds tighter than `?:` in C, so this already parses correctly.
clarifyCalculation:src/script.c:523
# `m->scale` is an int, so the product is computed as a double before it is
# stored in a long double. The extra precision was never there to lose, and
# this only feeds a `>=` threshold. Reported by cppcheck 2.17, not by 2.21.
truncLongCastAssignment:src/units.c:46
# Emitted when a function has more branches than the default check level walks.
# It is an `information` message about analysis depth, not a finding, and the
# --enable list above does not ask for it. cppcheck 2.17 prints it anyway.
normalCheckLevelMaxBranches
# `i` is a loop index reused across the function. Intentional.
variableScope:src/units.c:61
